@HELP: Status Panel -- Fields                   !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
{  NP       }Where you type an action character.
{  JOBNAME  }The name of the job, started task or TSO user.
{  TYPE     }JOB for a batch job, STC for a started task, TSU for a TSO user.
{  JNUM     }The JES2 job number.
{  PRTY     }The JES2 priority, 0 to 15. Can be overtyped (topic 5).
{  QUEUE    }The queue the job is on: INPUT, EXECUTION, PRINT, XMIT, SETUP
}            or RECEIVE.
{  C        }The job class of a batch job.
{  POS      }The place of a waiting job among the jobs of its class.
{  HDN      }The number of the job's held output data sets.
{  DEST     }Where the output goes: LOCAL, or Rn for remote n. Can be
}            overtyped (topic 5).
{  SAFF     }The system the job is bound to, if it is bound to one.
{  ASYS     }The system the job is active on.
{  STAT     }HOLD if the job is held.
}
}  The ? command shows further fields of the jobs (next topic).
}
